      "writtenOn": "2023-11-24T10:05:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is an `std` environment, and virt only has access to the rust-crypto `nostd` crates for now. Taking the `nostd` crate might potentially cause conflicts with other crates that `virtualizationservice` depends on later for their common dependencies.\n\nMoreover, when it comes to parsing the chain into individual certificates, `x509_parser` appears to be more convenient as it returns the trailing slice in return. On the other hand, `x509_cert` always results in an [error](https://docs.rs/der/0.6.1/der/enum.ErrorKind.html#variant.TrailingData) wrapping its own data type.",
      "parentUuid": "3d0470f8_0cdb46c4",
      "revId": "4366e3f9136e312092bc1b249200ef1f45bb843e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
